<section xml:id="sec-student-loans-and-financing" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
    <title>Student Loans and Financing</title>
    <introduction>
        <statement>
            <p>
               You are a college student and you or someone you know is paying for that education. Some
                students have families that have saved up over time to pay for their college, while others
                are financing their college education using loans. It is important to understand how student
                loans work and the impact of taking out a student loan on your immediate future2. First we
                will practice. 
            </p>
            <p>
                <ol>
                    <li>
                        <p>
                             You need to borrow money from Alisyn. Alisyn agrees to lend you $500, but you will
                            accrue 1% interest every day.  
                            <ol marker="(a)">
                                <li>
                                    <p>
                                        Write an expression for the amount you owe after 10 days, and generalize it for <m>t</m>
                                        days as a function of <m>t</m>
                                    </p>
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                    <p>
                                        How much did you owe in interest alone?
                                    </p>
                                </li>
                            </ol> 
                        </p>

                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p>
                             Consult the link below to learn how the interest on student loans is calculated:
                           <url href="https://studentaid.gov/understand-aid/types/loans/interest-rates" /> 
                            Calculate and compare the interest owed on the following two loans:
                            <m>\textbf{Loan\, A}</m> 10 year loan with principal amount of $15,000 with interest at <m>7%</m>.
                        </p>
                        <ul>
                            <li>
                                <p>
                                     [<m>\textbf{Loan\, B}</m>] 10 year loan with principal amount of $15,000 with interest at 4%
                                </p>
                                <p>
                                    <me>
                                        \text{The Impact of Attending College Fifteen Years Apart:}
                                    </me>
                                    <me>
                                        \text{The Case of Hailey and Alison}
                                        
                                    </me>
                                    
                                    
                                </p>
                            </li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p>
                            Imagine the following scenario, Hailey attended college between 2010–2011. Alison is
                            planning to enroll in the fall of the current year and expects to graduate four years
                            later. Assume that the amount borrowed consists of 50% of the tuition
                        </p>
                        <p>
                            <ol marker="(a)">
                                <li>
                                    <p>
                                       Fill in the table below  
                                    </p>
                                    <table>
                                        <!-- <title></title> -->
                                          <tabular hallign="center" top="medium" bottom="medium" left="medium" right="medium">
                                            <row>
                                                <cell>Hailey and Alison</cell>
                                            </row>
                                            <row>
                                                <cell></cell>
                                                <cell>Hailey</cell>
                                                <cell>Alison</cell>
                                                <cell>Note</cell>
                                                
                                            </row>
                                            <row>
                                                <cell>Tuition</cell>
                                                <cell></cell>
                                                <cell></cell>
                                                <cell>You need to find this information</cell>
                                            </row>
                                            <row>
                                                <cell>Loan Amount</cell>
                                                <cell></cell>
                                                <cell></cell>
                                                <cell>Hailey and Alison borrowed the same percentage (50%) of tuition</cell>
                                            </row>
                                            <row>
                                                <cell>Loan Term</cell>
                                                <cell>10 years</cell>
                                                <cell>10 years</cell>
                                                <cell></cell>
                                            </row>
                                            <row>
                                                <cell>Interest Rate</cell>
                                                <cell>6.92%</cell>
                                                <cell>4.66%</cell>
                                                <cell></cell>
                                                <cell></cell>
                                            </row>
                                            <row>
                                                <cell>Monthly Payment</cell>
                                                <cell></cell>
                                                <cell></cell>
                                                <cell></cell>
                                                <cell></cell>
                                            </row>
                                            <row>
                                                <cell>Total Intrest Paid</cell>
                                                <cell></cell>
                                                <cell></cell>
                                                <cell></cell>
                                                <cell></cell>
                                            </row>
                                            <row>
                                                <cell>Cumulative Payments</cell>
                                                <cell></cell>
                                                <cell></cell>
                                                <cell></cell>
                                            </row>
                                        </tabular>
                                    </table>
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                    <p>
                                       In referring to Hailey and Alison who pays less in interest and by how much 
                                    </p>
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                    <p>
                                       After repaying their loans, what are the cumulative payments of Hailey and Alison? 
                                    </p>
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                    <p>
                                       In reference to the previous question, is this result in line with or contradictory
                                        to the interest rate each borrower got? 
                                    </p>
                                    <p>
                                        <me>
                                            \text{Same Tuition Different Interest Rates:}
                                        </me>
                                    </p>
                                    <p>
                                        <me>
                                            \text{The Case of R’moni and Logan}
                                        </me>
                                        
                                        
                                    </p>
                                </li>
                            </ol>
                        </p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p>
                            Imagine the following scenario. R’moni and Logan attended college concurrently. They
                            borrow a comparable sum of money. However, Logan received a lower interest rate on
                            his loan. Assume that the amount borrowed constitutes 50% of the tuition
                            <ol marker="(a)">
                                <li>
                                    <p>
                                        Fill in the table below
                                    </p>
                                
                        <table>
                            <!-- <title></title> -->
                            <tabular hallign="center" top="medium" bottom="medium" left="medium" right="medium">
                                <row>
                                    <cell>Hailey and Alison</cell>
                                </row>
                                <row>
                                    <cell></cell>
                                    <cell>Hailey</cell>
                                    <cell>Alison</cell>
                                    <cell>Note</cell>
                                    
                                </row>
                                <row>
                                    <cell>Tuition</cell>
                                    <cell></cell>
                                    <cell></cell>
                                    <cell>You need to find this information</cell>
                                </row>
                                <row>
                                    <cell>Loan Amount</cell>
                                    <cell></cell>
                                    <cell></cell>
                                    <cell>Hailey and Alison borrowed the same percentage (50%) of tuition</cell>
                                </row>
                                <row>
                                    <cell>Loan Term</cell>
                                    <cell>10 years</cell>
                                    <cell>10 years</cell>
                                    <cell></cell>
                                </row>
                                <row>
                                    <cell>Interest Rate</cell>
                                    <cell>6.92%</cell>
                                    <cell>4.66%</cell>
                                    <cell></cell>
                                    <cell></cell>
                                </row>
                                <row>
                                    <cell>Monthly Payment</cell>
                                    <cell></cell>
                                    <cell></cell>
                                    <cell></cell>
                                    <cell></cell>
                                </row>
                                <row>
                                    <cell>Total Intrest Paid</cell>
                                    <cell></cell>
                                    <cell></cell>
                                    <cell></cell>
                                    <cell></cell>
                                </row>
                                <row>
                                    <cell>Cumulative Payments</cell>
                                    <cell></cell>
                                    <cell></cell>
                                    <cell></cell>
                                </row>
                            </tabular>
                        </table>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <p>
                                 How much does Logan save in interest compared with R’moni? Is the amount significant?
                            </p>
                        </li>
                     </ol>
                        </p>
                    </li>
                </ol>
            </p>
        </statement>
    </introduction>
    
</section>